--source include/have_ndb.inc

# RONDB-978: full lifecycle of a user rate-limit entity through ndb_mgm.
#
# This exercises the "USER" mgm command family (SET/GET/LIST/ALTER/DROP) end to
# end. It is a regression test for three defects that made these commands
# unusable:
#   1. The client command parser discarded the sub-command token, so every
#      "USER <sub>" command failed to dispatch.
#   2. The server declared the wrong num_rows for USER GET / USER LIST, hanging
#      the client's socket read.
#   3. The kernel double-prefixed the internal "$username" on participant data
#      nodes (and on restart), so USER DROP / USER ALTER failed with error 709
#      on any node that had stored "$$username".
#
# The commands print variable ids/versions, so the data output is suppressed and
# the test relies on exit codes: any failing ndb_mgm invocation (missing
# --error) aborts the test.

--disable_result_log
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER SET alice --rate-per-sec=100"
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER GET alice"
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER LIST"
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER ALTER alice --rate-per-sec=200"
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER GET alice"
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER DROP alice"

# After the drop the user must be gone: GET now fails.
--error 255,65280
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "USER GET alice"
--enable_result_log

--echo USER lifecycle completed
